{"name":"Kiss Me More","hex":"#de6b86","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"},{"term":"more","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["comparative degree of many: in greater number.","comparative degree of much: in greater quantity, amount, or proportion."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["To a greater degree or extent. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Used to form the comparative form of adjectives and adverbs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/more"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kiss Me More","blocks":[{"text":"\"Kiss Me More\" is a song by American rapper and singer Doja Cat featuring American singer SZA from the former's third studio album Planet Her (2021). It was released on April 9, 2021, as the album's lead single through Kemosabe and RCA Records. \"Kiss Me More\" was written by the artists alongside producers Yeti Beats and Rogét Chahayed, as well as Tizhimself and Carter Lang, who both provided additional production, and Lukasz Gottwald. It has been described as a disco and rap influenced pop song."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b1/Doja_Cat_-_Kiss_Me_More.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss_Me_More","wikidata":"Q106421322"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss","wikidata":"Q7307"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/20/Kiss_Me_More_music_video_screenshot.png/250px-Kiss_Me_More_music_video_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/20/Kiss_Me_More_music_video_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/20/Kiss_Me_More_music_video_screenshot.png/250px-Kiss_Me_More_music_video_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Doja Cat (right, next to SZA) plays a video game mimicking the seductive journey towards the aliens' lair on Planet Her, which has a display of trapped male astronauts in the background.[31][35]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKiss_Me_More_music_video_screenshot.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a7/Doja_Cat_-_Kiss_Me_More_Remix.jpg/250px-Doja_Cat_-_Kiss_Me_More_Remix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Doja_Cat_-_Kis